# ============================================================
# B.R.I.D.G.E — Firebase CI / service-account environment
# Copy to: firebase.env   (used by GitHub Actions & functions/)
# NOT loaded by the browser. Keep secret.
# ============================================================

# For GitHub Actions deploy (FirebaseExtended/action-hosting-deploy):
# Create a service account (IAM & Admin > Service Accounts > firebase-adminsdk,
# or Project Settings > Service accounts > Generate new private key),
# paste the ENTIRE JSON into a GitHub secret named:
#   FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_BRIDGE
# (the suffix _BRIDGE must match the project-id uppercased with non-alnum -> _)

# If you run deploys from a machine, point to the downloaded key file:
GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=../.env/serviceAccountKey.json
FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=your-project-id
